zcomph::SWE	<Ge ett uttryck best}ende av operander och operatorer.
Operander:
  (a)	flyt-tal	Ex: 4711   666.42    -11147
  (b)	variabler	Ex: SUNE
  (c)	text-str{ngar	Ex: "Allan tar en kaka"

Operatorer:

 (a) mon{ra operatorer:

	BEGIN, (, -, +, ENTIER, \, IF, FOR, NOT, ', CONSTR, &, CALL,
	ARG, PART, ENTRY, PRINT, READ, RDOBJ, RDLINE, CLEAR, X, Y, NIL,
	TERPRI, COMMAND, ", TRUE, FALSE

 (b) bin{ra operatorer:

	:, (, nothing, :=, COMPARE, !, **, ^, /, +, -, MOD, =, <, >, AND,
	OR, ;, comma, ), \, THEN, ELSE, TO, DO, END

Avsluta uttrycket med operatorn END eller en tom rad.>
	NOR	<Gi et uttrykk som best}r av tall,
variabler, strenger("xxx") og operatorer.
Operatorer som kan ha operander til h|yre for seg:

& ' CALL ARG COMMAND PART ENTRY PRINT + - ENTIER COMPARE ** ^ * / + - MOD
= < > NOT AND OR := ; , | IF THEN ELSE FOR TO DO CONSTR : ( ( BEGIN

Operatorer som ikke tar operander:

READ RDOBJ RDLINE X Y NIL TRUE FALSE CLEAR

Operatorer som kan ha operander til venstre for seg:

: ( := COMPARE ! ** ^ * / + - MOD = < > AND OR ; , ) | THEN ELSE TO DO END

Avslutt uttrykket med END eller en blank linje.>
	ENG	<Please give an expression consisting of numbers
(floating point), variables, strings("xxx") and operators.

The right hand operators:

& ' CALL ARG COMMAND PART ENTRY PRINT + - ENTIER COMPARE ** ^ * / + - MOD
= < > NOT AND OR := ; , | IF THEN ELSE FOR TO DO CONSTR : ( ( BEGIN

The anadic operators:

READ RDOBJ RDLINE X Y NIL TRUE FALSE CLEAR

The left hand operators:

: ( := COMPARE ** ^ * / + - MOD = < > AND OR ; , ) | THEN ELSE TO DO END

Finish expression with END or an empty line.>
	GER	<Please give an expression consisting of numbers
(floating point), variables, strings("xxx") and operators.

The right hand operators:

& ' CALL ARG COMMAND PART ENTRY PRINT + - ENTIER COMPARE ** ^ * / + - MOD
= < > NOT AND OR := ; , | IF THEN ELSE FOR TO DO CONSTR : ( ( BEGIN

The anadic operators:

READ RDOBJ RDLINE X Y NIL TRUE FALSE CLEAR

The left hand operators:

: ( := COMPARE ** ^ * / + - MOD = < > AND OR ; , ) | THEN ELSE TO DO END

Finish expression with END or an empty line.>
	FRE	<Please give an expression consisting of numbers
(floating point), variables, strings("xxx") and operators.

The right hand operators:

& ' CALL ARG COMMAND PART ENTRY PRINT + - ENTIER COMPARE ** ^ * / + - MOD
= < > NOT AND OR := ; , | IF THEN ELSE FOR TO DO CONSTR : ( ( BEGIN

The anadic operators:

READ RDOBJ RDLINE X Y NIL TRUE FALSE CLEAR

